      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name} I'm fine with that being the case, but can you add the warning back to the SDK in that case? Historically it used to give a warning if you had duplicate objects and offer to rename them for you. That option disappeared a while back - though if that was removed because it was what caused massive lag when focussing the Builder tab on larger worlds I can understand. If that's the case, how about adding that functionality back to another part of the SDK like the Network ID window?\n\nI'll see if I can recreate the issue on the new SDK with the network IDs all unique (as I've renamed everything now). I'm a little apprehensive about changing the prefab for hundreds of objects on a live project (and it's too large to easily clone) to retest.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
